            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0253" n="151" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg151"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2648/8–9.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Chargé Fletcher to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1907-10-22"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">October 22, 1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 767.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to report that the
                    legation is in receipt of a note from the foreign office, dated October 14,
                    1907, copy inclosed, informing it of the promulgation by the Chinese Government
                    of a new set of Mining Regulations, in two volumes, copies of which accompanied
                    the note. A translation, now being made, will be forwarded at a later date.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry P.
                    Fletcher.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d172-a1.xml" xpointer="d172-a1"/>
            </div>
